+    "field": "content_html",
+    "find": "<p data-narration-id=\"n14\">Your 19th-century novel question may offer a choice between an extract-based task and a discursive task, both assessing AO1, AO2 and AO3. <strong>Extract-based:</strong> Analyse the passage closely (language, imagery, symbolism), then connect to the novella as a whole. <strong>Discursive:</strong> Build an argument responding to a statement with evidence from across the text. Both require integrated AO1+AO2+AO3 in every paragraph. Check your exam board’s specimen paper for the exact format, mark weightings and timing.</p>",
+    "replace": "<p data-narration-id=\"n14\">For the 19th-century novel, choose one of two 40-mark extract-based questions. The paper is closed book. Analyse the printed passage closely, then connect it to the novella as a whole. Marks reward a critical response, textual evidence, analysis of Stevenson’s methods, relevant context and accurate spelling, punctuation, grammar, vocabulary and sentence structure.</p>",
