+    "field": "content_html",
+    "find": "The novella uses a complex narrative structure with <dfn class=\"term\" data-def=\"A story told through several different narrators, each providing a partial view. Stevenson uses Utterson, Enfield, Lanyon, and Jekyll as narrators.\">multiple perspectives</dfn>. The first eight chapters follow Utterson’s investigation. Chapter 9 is Dr Lanyon’s narrative. Chapter 10 is ‘Henry Jekyll’s Full Statement of the Case.’ Each narrator sees only part of the truth; only when combined do they reveal the whole picture.",
+    "replace": "The novella uses a complex narrative structure with <dfn class=\"term\" data-def=\"A story told through different narrative voices and viewpoints, each providing a partial view.\">multiple perspectives</dfn>. An anonymous third-person narrator follows Utterson’s investigation through most of the first eight chapters. Chapter 9 is Dr Lanyon’s first-person narrative, and Chapter 10 is ‘Henry Jekyll’s Full Statement of the Case.’ Each stage offers only part of the truth; together they reveal the whole picture.",
