+    "severity": "HIGH",
+    "note": "F24: Correct the recall prompt."
+  },
+  {
+    "lesson": 6,
+    "field": "content_html",
+    "find": "<p>Three narrators: Utterson sees external evidence but not the truth; Lanyon witnesses the transformation and dies; Jekyll provides the full interior confession. Each perspective is partial. Only together do they reveal the whole story. This mirrors Victorian society’s fragmented understanding of the self.</p>",
+    "replace": "<p>Three main stages: anonymous third-person narration follows Utterson’s external investigation; Lanyon’s first-person account witnesses the transformation; Jekyll’s first-person statement gives the interior confession. Each viewpoint is partial. Together they reveal the whole story.</p>",
+    "severity": "HIGH",
