+      "field": "content_html",
+      "severity": "MEDIUM",
+      "claim": "early Freud ... questioning the unity of the self [in the 1880s]",
+      "truth": "Freud’s psychoanalytic model belongs mainly to the 1890s and later. William James is an appropriate contemporary reference for 1880s debates about consciousness.",
+      "evidence": "Publication chronology: William James’s psychology work appeared through the 1870s–1880s; Freud’s psychoanalytic work developed in the 1890s.",
+      "verdict": "FIX"
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "F13",
+      "lesson": 3,
+      "field": "content_html",
+      "severity": "HIGH",
+      "claim": "the hand glimpsed on the stair is ‘dwarfish’ and ‘hairy’, and a servant girl saw a creature ‘crying out like a rat’",
+      "truth": "Poole cites the altered voice, the figure’s dwarfish build and its light, odd footsteps. No servant girl reports a hairy hand or a creature crying like a rat.",
+      "evidence": "Primary text ch. 8, lines 2875–2883, 2951–2959 and 3067–3089.",
+      "verdict": "FIX"
