+    "find": "He produces a letter signed by Hyde absolving him of blame. Utterson’s clerk, Mr Guest, compares the handwriting to Jekyll’s own and declares it a forgery — the letter Jekyll wrote <em>as Hyde</em> matches Jekyll’s hand in every feature except the slope. Stevenson plants <dfn class=\"term\" data-def=\"Clues given to the reader to suggest or hint at later events.\">foreshadowing</dfn>: the handwriting is literally the same because the writer is.",
+    "replace": "He produces a letter signed by Hyde, reassuring Jekyll that Hyde has a means of escape. Utterson’s clerk, Mr Guest, compares its handwriting with Jekyll’s and says that the two hands are largely identical but differently sloped. Utterson then suspects that Jekyll forged the letter for Hyde. Stevenson plants <dfn class=\"term\" data-def=\"Clues given to the reader to suggest or hint at later events.\">foreshadowing</dfn>: the resemblance hints at a connection between the two men.",
